## Out of scope, named and counted: `verification/probes/`

The scan's search root is `bench/` alone. `verification/probes/` holds **sixteen** files
in exactly this class — they open a real index and run raw SQL against `meta`,
`passages`, `passages_fts`:

    corpus-language-mix.mjs          keeping-diacritics-real-cost.mjs
    degenerate-real-index.mjs        lang_census.py
    diacritic-collision-cost.mjs     migrate-real-index.mjs
    droplist-adapts-to-corpus.mjs    scan-shape-v190-vs-fused.mjs
    expansion-penalties-probe.mjs    snippet-droplist-probe.mjs
    expansion-reach-probe.mjs        stoplist-cross-language.mjs
    folding-cost-and-benefit.mjs     vocab-scan-cost.mjs
    keeping-diacritics-cost.mjs      x4_probe_vocabulary.py

Counted, not estimated: the same predicates run over that root, with the identical run
over `bench/` as the positive control (it returns the 22-file inventory the merge request
records — 21 at filing, plus `bench/acceptance/adapters/zoteus.py` on arrival — the four
newly-classified files included). A review of PR #232 reported fifteen;
the run above returns sixteen, and the list is what the number is.

Deferred rather than done, deliberately. Several of these are one-off instruments pinned
to the pre-rename generation the way `bench/vec_real_measure.mjs` is, so classifying them
is 0101's per-driver judgement made sixteen more times — its own exercise. Sixteen reasons
written in a hurry to keep a suite green would be sixteen bare names with a longer type,
which is precisely what `EXCUSED` exists against. `verification/probes/` is in the repo's
lint gate for the reason the Makefile states — a probe that produced a committed figure is
code we depend on — so extending the root is the right eventual move, taken as a decision
rather than as a rider.

No new ticket: ID allocation was collision-prone this session (`erg new` offered 0602 with
0599-0601 already on an open merge request), and this sits below the severity floor as
filed. Recording it here keeps it findable without minting an ID.

The scope claim is machine-checked meanwhile. `SEARCH_ROOT` and `UNSEARCHED_ROOT` are
module constants; `test_the_search_root_is_the_one_the_module_documents` fails if either
moves without the docstring, `test_the_inventory_stays_inside_the_search_root` fails if the
walk escapes, and `test_a_matching_file_outside_the_search_root_is_not_named` puts the same
driver byte-for-byte inside and outside the root and asserts only one is named. A widening
therefore reds three tests by name instead of silently changing what the module claims.

## The guard fired on real traffic before it merged — an unplanned positive control

Recorded here because it is stronger evidence than anything staged in this ticket, and
because it happened by accident rather than by design.

While this merge request was open, `97d1490` ("Ticket 0579: goal 2's gates, asserted
over the same seven verbs") landed on `main` and took
`bench/acceptance/adapters/zoteus.py` across the class boundary: +143/-2 lines, and that
file from 0 occurrences of `sqlite3` and 0 of `FROM meta` to 4 and 2. `d81584c` ("Arm
R23's two directions…") then added a further +43/-2, taking `sqlite3` to 5 and leaving
`FROM meta` unchanged; over the whole range `5d2514d..8a5ad06` the file gained 184 lines,
0 -> 5 and 0 -> 2. Neither commit is an ancestor of this branch's base `5d2514d`.

An earlier round of this ticket, of the guard module and of the merge request attributed
the whole crossing to `d81584c` alone, with the range's numbers. That was wrong, and it
propagated through every reader of the thread before one ran `git show --stat d81584c`.
The finding is untouched by the correction — only the SHA and three numbers were — but
the correction is recorded here rather than quietly applied, because a load-bearing claim
nobody executed is the defect this repository keeps re-finding, and this one shipped
inside the machinery written against it.

So a genuine index-opening driver ARRIVED in
the repository, from another lane, with nobody staging it for this guard — which is
precisely the event the ticket was filed against, in precisely the manner the ticket
predicted (silently, in a file the roster had never heard of).

The branch was green on its own base and red the moment current `main` was merged in:

```
AssertionError: bench files that open a zoteus-built index and are in neither
DRIVERS (tests/test_index_schema_fixtures.py) nor EXCUSED:
{'bench/acceptance/adapters/zoteus.py': ['meta']}
```

Two things follow, and the second is the reason this is written down.

**The guard works on traffic, not only on fixtures.** Every other control in this ticket
is synthetic: a driver written into a `tmp_path` tree by the same hand that wrote the
scan, which proves the scan is capable of naming an arrival but not that a real arrival
looks like the fixture. This one was authored by a different lane for a different
purpose and named on the first run. A synthetic control shows the probe can fire; only
this shows it fires on the thing it was built for.

**It also exposed the gap this ticket had left open.** The guard caught a file ENTERING
the class. It would not have caught the identical change made INSIDE `EXCUSED` — an
already-excused file quietly starting to read a table its written reason was never about
— because `test_no_excused_entry_is_stale` fires only when a file LEAVES the class. That
asymmetry is the same shape as the one this ticket exists to fix, one level down. It is
closed here: each `EXCUSED` entry now pins the table set its reason was written against
(`Excuse.tables`), and `test_no_excused_entry_drifts_from_its_pinned_tables` reds by name
when a pin and the tree disagree, with `tmp_path` controls for a gained table, a lost
table, and the file-is-gone case that belongs to the staleness check instead.

`bench/acceptance/adapters/zoteus.py` is classified excused, on the substrate reason that
excuses `bench/smoke_upstream.py` — it is that file's `_restamp_and_open` moved into an
acceptance adapter, and its whole SQL surface is three statements on `meta.schemaVersion`
whose point is to write a version upstream must refuse. It is NOT excused for being
Python; see the retraction below.

## The structural Python argument is retracted

An earlier draft of the module argued that a Python driver is structurally outside a
`.mjs` gate, so rostering one would force a second Python mirror of the schema constants.
The premise was measured and is false: all four Python drivers in the inventory already
spawn `node` themselves (`Server(["node", …])`), so reaching the gate needs a subprocess
shim, not a mirror. The real obstacle is a hardcoded `["node", …]` in
`test_index_schema_fixtures.py::run_driver` — a suffix dispatch, a few lines.

It is retracted explicitly rather than dropped quietly because the fourth file is also
Python. Had that argument been load-bearing, every Python driver that ever arrives would
be excusable by the same sentence, and the excused class would be empty of judgement —
closed by construction rather than by measurement, which is the failure this ticket was
filed against. None of the four excuses rests on it.

For the record, since a harsher framing of this ticket circulated: the guard did not
declare its own class empty. The inventory is 22 files — 8 rostered and driven against
both fixture generations, 14 excused, and 11 of those 14 are ticket 0101's pre-existing
rulings restated as reasons. Four files were newly excused across the life of this
ticket, three at filing and the fourth on arrival.

## Invariants

- No bench driver is modified: this ticket adds a guard and classifies, it does not
  change a measurement.
- 0101's curated exclusions survive as reasons rather than being discarded.
- The check stays pure Python — no `node`, no subprocess, no database — so it cannot
  skip.
- The derivation is not allowed to go vacuous: an empty vocabulary or an unparsed roster
  fails loudly rather than passing on nothing.
- The search root cannot widen silently: it is a constant with tests on it, so reaching
  `verification/probes/` is a deliberate edit that reds three named tests.

## Exit criteria

- [x] A derived-inventory scan names every bench file that opens a zoteus-built index.
- [x] Every file it names is rostered in `DRIVERS` or excused with a non-blank written
      reason; blank, absent and stale entries are each refused, each with a control.
- [x] The three files above are classified, with the reasoning in the docstring — and so
      is the fourth, `bench/acceptance/adapters/zoteus.py`, which arrived on `main` while
      this merge request was open and was named by the guard itself.
- [x] An excuse cannot outlive the file it describes: each `EXCUSED` entry pins the table
      set its reason was written against, and a drift in either direction reds by name.
- [x] The red controls above are captured as terminal transcripts in the merge request,
      not paraphrased.
- [x] `make check` green and `./tickets/erg check tickets/` passes against
      `origin/main`'s ticket set.
- [x] The search root is a named constant, documented, and asserted — so the module
      cannot be read wider than it is.
